# Keep the tex source and markdown
!*.tex
!*.md

# Life tables ARE committed (exception to the data-is-gitignored policy above)
# so collaborators get the full input set from a clone. UN WPP E(x), 1990-2100,
# all 204 GBD nations. Generated by util_fetch_un_lifetables_bulk.R (no token
# needed; preferred) or util_download_un_lifetables.R (Data Portal API).
!data/lifetables/*_lifetable.csv

# Published benchmark values ARE committed, for the same reason: they are small,
# they are reference data rather than inputs, and a comparison is only auditable
# if the numbers it compares against are under version control.
!data/benchmarks/*.csv
# Large data lives at /var/home/aoz/data/wb-temp-attr-projections/ and is
# symlinked into place (since 2026-08-14). No trailing slash on these rules:
# `dir/` matches only real directories, not the symlinks now at these paths.
data/cmip6-scratch
data/erf
data/gbd-forecasts
data/shapefiles/gadm-colombia/
data/shapefiles/colombia_divipola_admin1.gpkg
data/temperature/cckp/
data/erf/cache/
output/cckp_run_manifest.csv
output/cckp_burden_manifest.csv

# Personal notes and meeting prep — not for collaborators
aoz-notes.org
samuel-meeting-agenda.md

# Duplicate / stale scratch (no trailing slash: now a symlink into ~/data)
GBD2023 Shape
daily-cmip6-download (1).R
heatwaves/

# Emacs autosaves / backup files (note: leading # must be escaped or git
# treats the whole line as a comment)
\#*\#
.\#*

# Copyrighted / not-for-redistribution references
from-samuel/burkart-paper.txt
gbd/gbd-appendix.txt

# Shapefile dir clutter — symlinks into the duplicate GBD2023 Shape/ tree,
# auxiliary metadata (.CPG, .shp.xml, etc.), and one-off test scripts. The
# canonical GBD shapefile is downloaded fresh per user; nothing here should
# be tracked except .gitkeep.
data/shapefiles/GBD2023_mapping_final.*
data/shapefiles/test-gbd-*
data/shapefiles/*.xml
data/shapefiles/*.CPG
data/mortality/citation.txt

# machine-specific run settings (see run_env.sh.example)
run_env.sh
output/logs/
*.nav
*.snm
data/era5_sd
